] [17592186508750 #edb/ref 1080 "$$74\\,681$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508750 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508750 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e2b5a82a-32f7-56ee-bf17-a5cd9187194a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508770 #edb/ref 1080 "$$5\\,067$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508770 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508770 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "edac4472-e23d-5e0d-afbb-78d7587dfad4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508810 #edb/ref 1080 "$$1\\,024$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508810 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508810 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ff6283c6-2d8e-5486-863d-299a65917ed1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508835 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508417 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508835 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508835 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508835 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508550 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508835 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508835 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508835 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508835 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186508498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508835 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "51810a08-334f-5c26-a631-f9e234750786" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508864 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508864 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508864 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508864 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508864 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508750 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508864 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508864 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508864 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186508750 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508864 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "98fc00d4-eaa0-5074-a7a2-52d9b8beb28f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508867 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508637 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508867 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508867 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508867 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508732 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508867 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508810 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508867 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508867 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508867 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186508708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508867 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a6663f5d-bdaf-51e5-a9ac-ff63ad1ed5e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508920 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508920 #edb/ref 1069 "q-63874" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508920 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508920 #edb/ref 1071 "Olivia bought a home for $$150\\,000.$ The value of the home declined by $16%$ annually. To the nearest dollar, what was the value of the home after $4$ years?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508920 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "38f4d55c-c716-54e2-ab1e-afc12e3f81f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508920 #edb/ref 1074 "The number $16%$ (expressed as a decimal) is equal to $0.16.$ Therefore, a decrease of $16%$ corresponds to multiplication by a factor of:\n\n$$\n1-0.16=0.84\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- After $1$ year, value of the home was $150\\,000\\cdot (0.84)$ dollars.\n\n- After $2$ years, value of the home was $150\\,000\\cdot (0.84)^{2}$ dollars.\n\n- After $3$ years, value of the home was  $150\\,000\\cdot (0.84)^{3}$ dollars.\n\n- After $4$ years, value of the home was $150\\,000\\cdot (0.84)^{4}$ dollars.\n\nEvaluating the last expression gives:\n\n$$\n150\\,000\\cdot (0.84)^{4}≈74\\,681\n$$\n\nSo, the home was worth $$74\\,681$ (to the nearest dollar) after $4$ years." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508964 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508867 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508964 #edb/ref 1069 "q-45481" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508964 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508964 #edb/ref 1071 "The price of a new bicycle is $$625.$ If the bicycle loses $\\frac{1}{5}$ of its value every year, what will be its value after $4$ years?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508964 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a3a40784-83f5-5659-8e12-9e2f515c5795" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508964 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the value of the bicycle reduces by $\\frac{1}{5}$ per year, $\\frac{4}{5}$ of its value remains every year. \n\nLet's calculate the value of the bicycle after every year:\n\n- After $1$ year, the bicycle will be worth $625\\cdot (\\frac{4}{5})$ dollars.\n\n- After $2$ years, the bicycle will be worth $625\\cdot {(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2}$ dollars.\n\n- After $3$ years, the bicycle will be worth $625\\cdot {(\\frac{4}{5})}^{3}$ dollars.\n\n- After $4$ years, the bicycle will be worth $625\\cdot {(\\frac{4}{5})}^{4}$ dollars.\n\nEvaluating the last expression, we get\n\n$$\n625\\cdot {(\\frac{4}{5})}^{4}=256.\n$$\n\nSo after $4$ years, the bicycle will be worth $$256.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508989 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508989 #edb/ref 1069 "q-26244" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508989 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508989 #edb/ref 1071 "A pest controller was responsible for humanely reducing the number of mice within a hotel. If there were $720$ mice initially and $\\frac{5}{6}$ of mice were removed from the hotel every day, how many mice remained in the hotel after two days?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508989 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e2edca84-13da-5da7-b4b8-ed4b37f13789" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508989 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the number of mice reduced by $\\frac{5}{6}$ per day, then only $\\frac{1}{6}$ of the mice from the previous day remained.\n\nSo we have:\n\n- At the start, there were $720$ mice.\n\n- After $1$ day, there were $720\\cdot (\\frac{1}{6})$ mice.\n\n- After $2$ days, there were $720\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{6})}^{2}$ mice.\n\nEvaluating the last expression, we get\n\n$$\n720\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{6})}^{2}=20.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $2$ days only $20$ mice remained." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
